tags: recursion-hops

A limit of the node: the most nodes that one request can go into, with the receiver.

The value is an integer in nodes. Example: 16. A larger remaining_hops in a request becomes the value. An absent remaining_hops is the value.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=recursion-hops
per=one request: RecursionGuard.remaining_hops, TunnelRequest.remaining_hops, BalanceStatementRequest.remaining_hops
rule=A larger remaining_hops in a request becomes the value. An absent remaining_hops is the value.
scope=none
unit=nodes
